{
  "channel": {
    "channel_id": "pharmacy-frontdesk-standardisation-2311",
    "threads": [
      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current issues and approve target workflow scope",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's kick off the 'Standardising Pharmacy Front-of-House Workflow' project. To get started on T1, could everyone please share the biggest pain points you face in the current front-of-house workflow? Think about everything from when a customer arrives to when they leave.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "wave",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 12454,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Finding medications quickly is a big one for me. Especially when there's a queue. Also, the handover process when one person takes the prescription and another dispenses it can be really messy.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 55101,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "From a shelf filling side, when assistants put customer returns in the wrong baskets, it means we sometimes put things back in the wrong place. That causes problems for everyone later.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "nod",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 255566,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Good points. I'd also add that we give inconsistent advice for over-the-counter products, which is a risk. And managing the queue gets stressful when we're searching for an item that's not where it should be.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Thanks all, this is very helpful. I'm capturing these. So far we have:\n1. Slow item retrieval\n2. Messy prescription handover\n3. Incorrect placement of returns\n4. Inconsistent OTC advice\n5. Poor queue management\nAnything else to add?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 32339,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "The phone is always ringing when I'm trying to help a customer. It's very distracting.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "@32339 That's a valid point about interruptions. We can add 'managing interruptions' to our list of challenges. For this project, let's focus on the core tasks we can define in the new workflow document, A1.",
            "mentions": [
              32339
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 20729,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "I agree with the point about returns. It makes the stock checks much harder than they need to be.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 12454,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "So what are we going to fix first? I think making things faster is the most important.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "Based on what impacts safety and customer experience the most, I suggest we prioritize these three pain points: 1. Slow item retrieval (safety risk), 2. Inconsistent OTC advice (compliance risk), and 3. Messy prescription handover (dispensing error risk). Does everyone agree on these as our top three to address first?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 255566,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "That makes sense. Those three cause the most significant problems day-to-day.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 55101,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "Ok with me.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 12454,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "+1",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "Great. Now for the overall scope. For the new workflow document (A1), I propose we standardize the following processes: prescription intake, OTC query handling, payment processing, dispensing and handover, and handling stock returns to the front-of-house. Is anything critical missing?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M15",
            "speaker_id": 255566,
            "reply_to": "M14",
            "text": "Should we explicitly include the click-and-collect process in that list? It has its own quirks.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M16",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": "M15",
            "text": "Good call. Yes, let's add that. Any other thoughts?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M17",
            "speaker_id": 20729,
            "reply_to": "M16",
            "text": "Looks good to me.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M18",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": "M17",
            "text": "Okay, locking this in. We've agreed on the scope of processes to be standardised (D1) and our top three pain points to address (D2). I'll start drafting the current state map for T1 based on this discussion. Thanks everyone.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
