            "speaker_id": 12454,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Just scanned A5, the checklist looks straightforward. I can do that.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 84286,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Thanks @255566, this is a great start. For the stock reception SOP in A1, can we add a mandatory double-check step for controlled drugs and high-value items, signed by two people? It's a key compliance point. For the daily checklist A5, it looks good, but we should add a specific check for 'look-alike, sound-alike' (LASA) medications to ensure they are properly separated.",
            "mentions": [
              255566
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 55101,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "The daily checklist in A5 seems long. The time estimate per aisle seems a bit short. It might take me longer, especially at the start.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 255566,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Good points. @84286 I'll add the two-person sign-off for high-risk items to the SOP in A1 and the LASA check to A5. @55101 you're right, the time is just an estimate. We can adjust it after we test it for a week as per the T9 definition of done. The main thing is to get the checks done correctly.",
